      "content": "You are correct that framing the era as \"colonial violence\" might feel jarring or overly academic for many visitors seeking traditional narratives of national growth. However, omitting this context entirely risks creating a one-sided history that overlooks the actual human cost of that progress. A more effective strategy could be to weave the reality of displacement into the story of discovery, using poignant imagery to show how the two threads—achievement and sacrifice—are inextricably linked. This approach honors the spirit of the West without erasing the painful truths that shaped the modern nation.",
